RetroBoot: Quadra ADB autopolling at the Macintosh II rate with input, slower while idle (m68k series).

mac_via autopolls the ADB devices every 20 ms and each empty poll is several
VIA1 shift-register interrupts: about 250 of the 316 interrupts a second at
an idle Mac OS 8.1 Finder, while an ADB mouse moved the pointer at most 50
times a second.  mos6522-q800-via1 properties: adb-poll-ms (default 11, the
Macintosh II family's ADB Manager rate; 0 keeps 20) is the period while
there is input; adb-idle-poll-ms (default 100; 0 = off) is the period once no
device has had input for adb-idle-after-ms (default 1000).  Input to the ADB
keyboard or mouse polls at once and restores adb-poll-ms.  The settings
live in the VIA's state and reach the bus at realize (qbus_init() in the
VIA's instance_init zeroes the bus after the property defaults are set),
the bus's own reset restores the VIA's period instead of 20 ms, and a new
autopoll mask (Mac OS talks to each device in turn) waits the idle period
too.  Lab, idle Mac OS 8.1 Finder: 105 autopolls a second -> 10.

